      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 11**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>src/components/Form/CVCFieldForm.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-20`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**CVC 길이 규칙 값(3) 중복 관리로 드리프트 위험이 있습니다.**\n\nLine 18의 `fieldMaxLength={3}`와 validator 내부 규칙이 분리되면, 한쪽만 수정될 때 불일치가 생길 수 있습니다.  \n`길이 규칙을 단일 상수로 모을 수 있을지` 한번 점검해보실래요?\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/Form/CVCFieldForm.tsx` around lines 18 - 20, Extract the\nhard-coded CVC length into a single exported constant (e.g., CVC_MAX_LENGTH) and\nuse that constant for both the fieldMaxLength prop in CVCFieldForm and inside\nthe cvcValidator logic so the length rule is defined in one place; update\nreferences to the numeric literal in the CVCFieldForm component and in the\nvalidator implementation to use the new constant (ensure the constant is\nimported if moved to a shared file).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/components/CardPreview/CardPreview.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-25`: _💤 Low value_\n\n**`cardNumbersToBrand` 함수를 컴포넌트 외부로 분리하거나 `useMemo`로 최적화 고려**\n\n이 함수는 순수 함수이므로 컴포넌트 외부에 정의하면 매 렌더링마다 재생성되는 것을 방지할 수 있습니다. 또는 브랜드 판별 로직이 `src/utils/validate.ts`의 `validateCardBrandNumber`와 유사하므로, 중복을 줄이기 위해 통합을 고려해 보세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardPreview/CardPreview.tsx` around lines 13 - 25, The\ncardNumbersToBrand function is recreated on every render; move this pure helper\nout of the CardPreview component (e.g., export it from the same module or a\nutils file) or wrap its usage in useMemo so it isn’t redefined each render, and\nconsider reusing or delegating to the existing validateCardBrandNumber utility\nto avoid duplicate brand-detection logic; update references to\ncardNumbersToBrand in the component accordingly and export or import\nvalidateCardBrandNumber where appropriate.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/utils/validate.ts (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`72-74`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**에러 메시지와 검증 로직 간 의미 불일치**\n\n`validateInputValueLength`는 `inputValue.length < inputMaxLength`일 때 `true`를 반환하고, 이때 `ERROR_MESSAGE.MAX_LENGTH`(\"숫자는 X자리를 입력해야 합니다\")가 표시됩니다.\n\n이 에러는 \"최대 길이 초과\" 상황이 아니라 \"필수 길이 미달\" 상황을 검증하는 것입니다. 함수명이나 에러 메시지 키를 `MIN_LENGTH` 또는 `REQUIRED_LENGTH`로 변경하면 의도가 더 명확해질 것입니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/utils/validate.ts` around lines 72 - 74, The function\nvalidateInputValueLength currently returns true when inputValue.length <\ninputMaxLength but is paired with ERROR_MESSAGE.MAX_LENGTH, causing a mismatch\nbetween logic and message; rename the function to something like\nvalidateInputValueMinLength or validateRequiredLength (or alternatively invert\nthe logic to check inputValue.length > inputMaxLength) and update all callers\nand the error key usage (e.g., replace ERROR_MESSAGE.MAX_LENGTH with\nERROR_MESSAGE.MIN_LENGTH or ERROR_MESSAGE.REQUIRED_LENGTH) so the function name,\nboolean semantics, and error message key consistently reflect \"minimum/required\nlength\" validation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`69-74`: _💤 Low value_\n\n**함수 이름과 반환값의 의미가 직관적이지 않습니다**\n\n`validateNaN`과 `validateInputValueLength` 함수들이 \"유효하지 않을 때\" `true`를 반환합니다. 일반적인 컨벤션에서 `validate*` 또는 `isValid*`는 유효할 때 `true`를 반환합니다.\n\n현재 네이밍이 혼란을 줄 수 있는데, 이러한 상황에서 코드 가독성을 높이려면 어떤 접근법이 좋을까요? 예를 들어:\n- `isNaN` → `isNotNumeric` 또는 `containsNonNumeric`\n- `validateInputValueLength` → `isIncomplete` 또는 `isBelowMinLength`\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/utils/validate.ts` around lines 69 - 74, Rename the confusing validators\nso truthy return means \"valid\" (or use clear negative names) and update all\ncallers: change validateNaN to containsNonNumeric (or isNotNumeric) and\nvalidateInputValueLength to isBelowMinLength (or isIncomplete) so their boolean\nsemantics match the names; adjust implementations accordingly (invert return\nvalues if switching to positive semantics) in the functions validateNaN and\nvalidateInputValueLength, update any exports and import sites to the new names,\nand run tests/typechecks to ensure all usages (including any references in\ncomponents or helpers) are updated consistently.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/components/Common/Form/InputFieldForm.tsx (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`42-54`: _💤 Low value_\n\n**`Array.from` 대신 `numberList.map`을 직접 사용하는 것이 어떨까요?**\n\n`numberList`는 이미 배열이므로 `Array.from({ length: numberList.length }).map((_, index) => ...)`보다 `numberList.map((_, index) => ...)`가 더 직관적입니다.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ 간단한 개선 제안</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        {Array.from({ length: numberList.length }).map((_, index) => (\n+        {numberList.map((_, index) => (\n           <FormField\n             key={`${label}-${index}`}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/Form/InputFieldForm.tsx` around lines 42 - 54, Replace\nthe unnecessary Array.from length-mapping with a direct iteration over\nnumberList: change the expression that renders FormField components to use\nnumberList.map((value, index) => ...) instead of Array.from({ length:\nnumberList.length }).map(...), so you can pass the current item directly (use\nvalue instead of numberList[index]) and keep the same props (key, id, index,\nnumbers, fieldMaxLength, validator, onChange, placeholderArr[index],\nsetErrorMessage) to the FormField component.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`57-57`: _💤 Low value_\n\n**ErrorMessage 렌더링 로직 간소화 가능**\n\n현재 `{<ErrorMessage>{errorMessage.trim().length > 0 && errorMessage}</ErrorMessage>}`는 불필요하게 복잡합니다. 외부의 `{}` 중괄호도 불필요하고, trim 체크 후 원본 문자열을 다시 사용하는 것도 비효율적입니다.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ 간소화 제안</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      {<ErrorMessage>{errorMessage.trim().length > 0 && errorMessage}</ErrorMessage>}\n+      <ErrorMessage>{errorMessage.trim() || null}</ErrorMessage>\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/Form/InputFieldForm.tsx` at line 57, In InputFieldForm,\nsimplify the ErrorMessage rendering: remove the unnecessary outer JSX braces and\navoid calling trim() twice by computing or using errorMessage.trim() once in the\nconditional; render <ErrorMessage> only when the trimmed string is non-empty\n(use errorMessage.trim() in the condition and as the child) so the expression\nbecomes a direct conditional render tied to ErrorMessage and errorMessage.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/constants/index.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`25-25`: _💤 Low value_\n\n**`ERROR_MESSAGE.NAN`이 정의되었지만 사용되지 않습니다**\n\n`validate.ts`에서 `validateNaN` 함수는 존재하지만, 실제로 이 에러 메시지를 반환하는 validator가 없습니다. 이 상수를 사용할 계획이 있는지, 아니면 제거해야 하는지 검토해 보세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/constants/index.ts` at line 25, ERROR_MESSAGE.NAN is defined but never\nused; locate the validator function validateNaN in validate.ts and either (A)\nreplace any hard-coded \"숫자만 입력 가능합니다.\" messages with ERROR_MESSAGE.NAN and\nexport/use validateNaN where appropriate, or (B) if the NaN validator is not\nneeded, remove the ERROR_MESSAGE.NAN constant from src/constants/index.ts and\ndelete the unused validateNaN function to keep constants and validators in sync;\nensure references to ERROR_MESSAGE.NAN or validateNaN are updated accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Around line 29-46: Fix the Korean typo \"떄\" → \"때\" in the README checklist\nitems: replace in the three occurrences \"한 입력 폼의 입력된 번호의 개수가 4개 미만일 떄 포커스가 벗어난\n경우\", \"한 입력 폼의 입력된 번호의 개수가 2개 미만일 떄 포커스가 벗어난 경우\", and \"한 입력 폼의 입력된 번호의 개수가 3개 미만일\n떄 포커스가 벗어난 경우\" so each reads \"...개 미만일 때 포커스가 벗어난 경우\".\n\nIn `@src/App.tsx`:\n- Line 16: The style using width: 100vw can cause horizontal scroll because it\nincludes the scrollbar; update the component/style in App.tsx that currently\nsets width: 100vw to use width: 100% instead (locate the rule where width: 100vw\nis declared and replace it), ensuring any related layout expectations (e.g.,\ncontainer or root component) still behave as intended after the change.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardPreview/CardPreview.tsx`:\n- Line 1: Replace the incorrect import of styled in CardPreview.tsx (currently\nimporting from 'storybook/theming') with the app-appropriate package by\nimporting styled from '@emotion/styled' instead; update the import statement at\nthe top of the CardPreview component file so all usages of styled within the\nCardPreview component resolve to the same emotion-styled API used by other\ncomponents like InputFieldForm.tsx.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/ErrorMessage/ErrorMessage.tsx`:\n- Around line 8-10: The styled component Message (a span) in ErrorMessage.tsx is\ninline by default so the width/height rules won’t reliably apply; update the\nMessage styled definition to include a display property (e.g., display: block or\ndisplay: inline-block) so the width/height take effect and the layout behaves as\nintended.\n- Around line 4-6: ErrorMessage 컴포넌트가 동적 검증 메시지를 스